Subject: [PATCH] Borderless full screen: not always on top

raylib's ToggleBorderlessWindowed also sets GLFW_FLOATING (topmost): Alt+Tab brought no other
window in front of the game. The flag is cleared after it; a window the screen's size still
covers the taskbar while it is the one in front.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp
index 5d24a5c..c23e107 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp
@@ -66,6 +66,11 @@ static void setFullScreen(bool on)
 {
     if (on != IsWindowState(FLAG_BORDERLESS_WINDOWED_MODE))
         ToggleBorderlessWindowed();
+    // raylib's borderless window is also made always-on-top (GLFW_FLOATING): Alt+Tab then brought
+    // no other window in front of it. A window the screen's size still covers the taskbar while it
+    // is the one in front.
+    if (on && IsWindowState(FLAG_WINDOW_TOPMOST))
+        ClearWindowState(FLAG_WINDOW_TOPMOST);
     static const char *exactEnv = std::getenv("PS2X_FULLSCREEN_EXACT");
     const bool exact = (exactEnv && *exactEnv) ? *exactEnv != '0' : ps2_host_present::active();
     if (on && !exact)
-- 
